# Backend Rules

- Backend app lives in `server/`.
- Main entry file is `server/src/server.ts`.
- Main route aggregator is `server/src/routes/index.ts`.
- Use Express with TypeScript.
- Keep route handlers simple and readable.
- Use raw `pg` queries with parameterized values. Do not add an ORM.
- Database connection code belongs in `server/src/db/`.
- SQL migration files belong in `server/src/migrations/`.
- Repository files belong in `server/src/repository/`.
- Middleware belongs in `server/src/middleware/`.
- Shared helpers such as JWT, Google OAuth, OpenAI, and environment helpers belong in `server/src/lib/`.
- Do not add controllers/services folders unless an active spec explicitly asks.
- Do not hard-code secrets.
- Add required environment variables to `server/.env.example`.
- Keep errors beginner-readable. Avoid complex custom frameworks unless the active spec requires them.
